#: ../../source/request_README.md:152
msgid "Promises & Async/Await"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/request_README.md:154
msgid ""
"`request` supports both streaming and callback interfaces natively. If "
"you'd like `request` to return a Promise instead, you can use an "
"alternative interface wrapper for `request`. These wrappers can be useful"
" if you prefer to work with Promises, or if you'd like to use "
"`async`/`await` in ES2017."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/request_README.md:156
msgid ""
"Several alternative interfaces are provided by the request team, "
"including:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/request_README.md:157
msgid ""
"[`request-promise`](https://github.com/request/request-promise) (uses "
"[Bluebird](https://github.com/petkaantonov/bluebird) Promises)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/request_README.md:158
msgid ""
"[`request-promise-native`](https://github.com/request/request-promise-"
"native) (uses native Promises)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/request_README.md:159
msgid ""
"[`request-promise-any`](https://github.com/request/request-promise-any) "
"(uses [any-promise](https://www.npmjs.com/package/any-promise) Promises)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/request_README.md:161
msgid ""
"Also, "
"[`util.promisify`](https://nodejs.org/api/util.html#util_util_promisify_original),"
" which is available from Node.js v8.0 can be used to convert a regular "
"function that takes a callback to return a promise instead."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/request_README.md:170
msgid "Forms"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/request_README.md:172
msgid ""
"`request` supports `application/x-www-form-urlencoded` and `multipart"
"/form-data` form uploads. For `multipart/related` refer to the "
"`multipart` API."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/request_README.md:175
msgid "application/x-www-form-urlencoded (URL-Encoded Forms)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/request_README.md:177
msgid "URL-encoded forms are simple."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/request_README.md:188
msgid "multipart/form-data (Multipart Form Uploads)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/request_README.md:190
msgid ""
"For `multipart/form-data` we use the [form-data](https://github.com/form-"
"data/form-data) library by [@felixge](https://github.com/felixge). For "
"the most cases, you can pass your upload form data via the `formData` "
"option."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/request_README.md:225
msgid ""
"For advanced cases, you can access the form-data object itself via "
"`r.form()`. This can be modified until the request is fired on the next "
"cycle of the event-loop. (Note that this calling `form()` will clear the "
"currently set form data for that request.)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/request_README.md:235
msgid ""
"See the [form-data README](https://github.com/form-data/form-data) for "
"more information & examples."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/request_README.md:238
msgid "multipart/related"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/request_README.md:240
msgid ""
"Some variations in different HTTP implementations require a newline/CRLF "
"before, after, or both before and after the boundary of a "
"`multipart/related` request (using the multipart option). This has been "
"observed in the .NET WebAPI version 4.0. You can turn on a boundary "
"preambleCRLF or postamble by passing them as `true` to your request "
"options."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/request_README.md:282
msgid "HTTP Authentication"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/request_README.md:304
msgid "If passed as an option, `auth` should be a hash containing values:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/request_README.md:306
msgid "`user` || `username`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/request_README.md:307
msgid "`pass` || `password`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/request_README.md:308
msgid "`sendImmediately` (optional)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/request_README.md:309
msgid "`bearer` (optional)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/request_README.md:311
msgid ""
"The method form takes parameters `auth(username, password, "
"sendImmediately, bearer)`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/request_README.md:314
msgid ""
"`sendImmediately` defaults to `true`, which causes a basic or bearer "
"authentication header to be sent. If `sendImmediately` is `false`, then "
"`request` will retry with a proper authentication header after receiving "
"a `401` response from the server (which must contain a `WWW-Authenticate`"
" header indicating the required authentication method)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/request_README.md:320
msgid ""
"Note that you can also specify basic authentication using the URL itself,"
" as detailed in [RFC 1738](http://www.ietf.org/rfc/rfc1738.txt). Simply "
"pass the `user:password` before the host with an `@` sign:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/request_README.md:334
msgid ""
"Digest authentication is supported, but it only works with "
"`sendImmediately` set to `false`; otherwise `request` will send basic "
"authentication on the initial request, which will probably cause the "
"request to fail."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/request_README.md:338
msgid ""
"Bearer authentication is supported, and is activated when the `bearer` "
"value is available. The value may be either a `String` or a `Function` "
"returning a `String`. Using a function to supply the bearer token is "
"particularly useful if used in conjunction with `defaults` to allow a "
"single function to supply the last known token at the time of sending a "
"request, or to compute one on the fly."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/request_README.md:350
msgid "Custom HTTP Headers"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/request_README.md:352
msgid ""
"HTTP Headers, such as `User-Agent`, can be set in the `options` object. "
"In the example below, we call the github API to find out the number of "
"stars and forks for the request repository. This requires a custom `User-"
"Agent` header as well as https."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/request_README.md:384
msgid "OAuth Signing"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/request_README.md:386
msgid ""
"[OAuth version 1.0](https://tools.ietf.org/html/rfc5849) is supported. "
"The default signing algorithm is [HMAC-"
"SHA1](https://tools.ietf.org/html/rfc5849#section-3.4.2):"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/request_README.md:447
msgid ""
"For [RSA-SHA1 "
"signing](https://tools.ietf.org/html/rfc5849#section-3.4.3), make the "
"following changes to the OAuth options object:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/request_README.md:449
msgid "Pass `signature_method : 'RSA-SHA1'`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/request_README.md:450
msgid ""
"Instead of `consumer_secret`, specify a `private_key` string in [PEM "
"format](http://how2ssl.com/articles/working_with_pem_files/)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/request_README.md:453
msgid ""
"For [PLAINTEXT signing](http://oauth.net/core/1.0/#anchor22), make the "
"following changes to the OAuth options object:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/request_README.md:455
msgid "Pass `signature_method : 'PLAINTEXT'`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/request_README.md:457
msgid ""
"To send OAuth parameters via query params or in a post body as described "
"in The [Consumer Request "
"Parameters](http://oauth.net/core/1.0/#consumer_req_param) section of the"
" oauth1 spec:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/request_README.md:460
msgid ""
"Pass `transport_method : 'query'` or `transport_method : 'body'` in the "
"OAuth options object."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/request_README.md:462
msgid "`transport_method` defaults to `'header'`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/request_README.md:464
msgid ""
"To use [Request Body "
"Hash](https://oauth.googlecode.com/svn/spec/ext/body_hash/1.0/oauth-"
"bodyhash.html) you can either"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/request_README.md:465
msgid "Manually generate the body hash and pass it as a string `body_hash: '...'`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/request_README.md:466
msgid "Automatically generate the body hash by passing `body_hash: true`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/request_README.md:474
msgid "Proxies"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/request_README.md:476
msgid ""
"If you specify a `proxy` option, then the request (and any subsequent "
"redirects) will be sent via a connection to the proxy server."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/request_README.md:479
msgid ""
"If your endpoint is an `https` url, and you are using a proxy, then "
"request will send a `CONNECT` request to the proxy server *first*, and "
"then use the supplied connection to connect to the endpoint."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/request_README.md:483
msgid "That is, first it will make a request like:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/request_README.md:491
msgid ""
"and then the proxy server make a TCP connection to `endpoint-server` on "
"port `80`, and return a response that looks like:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/request_README.md:498
msgid ""
"At this point, the connection is left open, and the client is "
"communicating directly with the `endpoint-server.com` machine."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/request_README.md:501
msgid ""
"See [the wikipedia page on HTTP "
"Tunneling](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/HTTP_tunnel) for more "
"information."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/request_README.md:504
msgid ""
"By default, when proxying `http` traffic, request will simply make a "
"standard proxied `http` request. This is done by making the `url` section"
" of the initial line of the request a fully qualified url to the "
"endpoint."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/request_README.md:509
msgid "For example, it will make a single request that looks like:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/request_README.md:519
msgid ""
"Because a pure \"http over http\" tunnel offers no additional security or"
" other features, it is generally simpler to go with a straightforward "
"HTTP proxy in this case. However, if you would like to force a tunneling "
"proxy, you may set the `tunnel` option to `true`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/request_README.md:524
msgid ""
"You can also make a standard proxied `http` request by explicitly setting"
" `tunnel : false`, but **note that this will allow the proxy to see the "
"traffic to/from the destination server**."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/request_README.md:528
msgid ""
"If you are using a tunneling proxy, you may set the "
"`proxyHeaderWhiteList` to share certain headers with the proxy."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/request_README.md:531
msgid ""
"You can also set the `proxyHeaderExclusiveList` to share certain headers "
"only with the proxy and not with destination host."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/request_README.md:534
msgid "By default, this set is:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/request_README.md:563
msgid ""
"Note that, when using a tunneling proxy, the `proxy-authorization` header"
" and any headers from custom `proxyHeaderExclusiveList` are *never* sent "
"to the endpoint server, but only to the proxy server."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/request_README.md:568
msgid "Controlling proxy behaviour using environment variables"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/request_README.md:570
msgid "The following environment variables are respected by `request`:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/request_README.md:572
msgid "`HTTP_PROXY` / `http_proxy`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/request_README.md:573
msgid "`HTTPS_PROXY` / `https_proxy`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/request_README.md:574
msgid "`NO_PROXY` / `no_proxy`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/request_README.md:576
msgid ""
"When `HTTP_PROXY` / `http_proxy` are set, they will be used to proxy non-"
"SSL requests that do not have an explicit `proxy` configuration option "
"present. Similarly, `HTTPS_PROXY` / `https_proxy` will be respected for "
"SSL requests that do not have an explicit `proxy` configuration option. "
"It is valid to define a proxy in one of the environment variables, but "
"then override it for a specific request, using the `proxy` configuration "
"option. Furthermore, the `proxy` configuration option can be explicitly "
"set to false / null to opt out of proxying altogether for that request."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/request_README.md:578
msgid ""
"`request` is also aware of the `NO_PROXY`/`no_proxy` environment "
"variables. These variables provide a granular way to opt out of proxying,"
" on a per-host basis. It should contain a comma separated list of hosts "
"to opt out of proxying. It is also possible to opt of proxying when a "
"particular destination port is used. Finally, the variable may be set to "
"`*` to opt out of the implicit proxy configuration of the other "
"environment variables."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/request_README.md:580
msgid "Here's some examples of valid `no_proxy` values:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/request_README.md:582
msgid "`google.com` - don't proxy HTTP/HTTPS requests to Google."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/request_README.md:583
msgid ""
"`google.com:443` - don't proxy HTTPS requests to Google, but *do* proxy "
"HTTP requests to Google."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/request_README.md:584
msgid ""
"`google.com:443, yahoo.com:80` - don't proxy HTTPS requests to Google, "
"and don't proxy HTTP requests to Yahoo!"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/request_README.md:585
msgid "`*` - ignore `https_proxy`/`http_proxy` environment variables altogether."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/request_README.md:593
msgid "UNIX Domain Sockets"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/request_README.md:595
msgid ""
"`request` supports making requests to [UNIX Domain "
"Sockets](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Unix_domain_socket). To make one, "
"use the following URL scheme:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/request_README.md:602
msgid ""
"Note: The `SOCKET` path is assumed to be absolute to the root of the host"
" file system."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/request_README.md:610
msgid "TLS/SSL Protocol"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/request_README.md:612
msgid ""
"TLS/SSL Protocol options, such as `cert`, `key` and `passphrase`, can be "
"set directly in `options` object, in the `agentOptions` property of the "
"`options` object, or even in `https.globalAgent.options`. Keep in mind "
"that, although `agentOptions` allows for a slightly wider range of "
"configurations, the recommended way is via `options` object directly, as "
"using `agentOptions` or `https.globalAgent.options` would not be applied "
"in the same way in proxied environments (as data travels through a TLS "
"connection instead of an http/https agent)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/request_README.md:634
msgid "Using `options.agentOptions`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/request_README.md:636
msgid ""
"In the example below, we call an API that requires client side SSL "
"certificate (in PEM format) with passphrase protected private key (in PEM"
" format) and disable the SSLv3 protocol:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/request_README.md:661
msgid "It is able to force using SSLv3 only by specifying `secureProtocol`:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/request_README.md:672
msgid ""
"It is possible to accept other certificates than those signed by "
"generally allowed Certificate Authorities (CAs). This can be useful, for "
"example,  when using self-signed certificates. To require a different "
"root certificate, you can specify the signing CA by adding the contents "
"of the CA's certificate file to the `agentOptions`. The certificate the "
"domain presents must be signed by the root certificate specified:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/request_README.md:686
msgid ""
"The `ca` value can be an array of certificates, in the event you have a "
"private or internal corporate public-key infrastructure hierarchy. For "
"example, if you want to connect to https://api.some-server.com which "
"presents a key chain consisting of:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/request_README.md:687
msgid "its own public key, which is signed by:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/request_README.md:688
msgid "an intermediate \"Corp Issuing Server\", that is in turn signed by:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/request_README.md:689
msgid "a root CA \"Corp Root CA\";"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/request_README.md:691
msgid "you can configure your request as follows:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/request_README.md:710
msgid "Support for HAR 1.2"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/request_README.md:712
msgid ""
"The `options.har` property will override the values: `url`, `method`, "
"`qs`, `headers`, `form`, `formData`, `body`, `json`, as well as construct"
" multipart data and read files from disk when "
"`request.postData.params[].fileName` is present without a matching "
"`value`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/request_README.md:714
msgid ""
"A validation step will check if the HAR Request format matches the latest"
" spec (v1.2) and will skip parsing if not matching."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/request_README.md:759
msgid "request(options, callback)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/request_README.md:761
msgid ""
"The first argument can be either a `url` or an `options` object. The only"
" required option is `uri`; all others are optional."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/request_README.md:763
msgid ""
"`uri` || `url` - fully qualified uri or a parsed url object from "
"`url.parse()`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/request_README.md:764
msgid ""
"`baseUrl` - fully qualified uri string used as the base url. Most useful "
"with `request.defaults`, for example when you want to do many requests to"
" the same domain. If `baseUrl` is `https://example.com/api/`, then "
"requesting `/end/point?test=true` will fetch "
"`https://example.com/api/end/point?test=true`. When `baseUrl` is given, "
"`uri` must also be a string."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/request_README.md:765
msgid "`method` - http method (default: `\"GET\"`)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/request_README.md:766
#, python-brace-format
msgid "`headers` - http headers (default: `{}`)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/request_README.md:770
msgid "`qs` - object containing querystring values to be appended to the `uri`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/request_README.md:771
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"`qsParseOptions` - object containing options to pass to the "
"[qs.parse](https://github.com/hapijs/qs#parsing-objects) method. "
"Alternatively pass options to the "
"[querystring.parse](https://nodejs.org/docs/v0.12.0/api/querystring.html#querystring_querystring_parse_str_sep_eq_options)"
" method using this format `{sep:';', eq:':', options:{}}`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/request_README.md:772
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"`qsStringifyOptions` - object containing options to pass to the "
"[qs.stringify](https://github.com/hapijs/qs#stringifying) method. "
"Alternatively pass options to the  "
"[querystring.stringify](https://nodejs.org/docs/v0.12.0/api/querystring.html#querystring_querystring_stringify_obj_sep_eq_options)"
" method using this format `{sep:';', eq:':', options:{}}`. For example, "
"to change the way arrays are converted to query strings using the `qs` "
"module pass the `arrayFormat` option with one of "
"`indices|brackets|repeat`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/request_README.md:773
msgid ""
"`useQuerystring` - if true, use `querystring` to stringify and parse "
"querystrings, otherwise use `qs` (default: `false`). Set this option to "
"`true` if you need arrays to be serialized as `foo=bar&foo=baz` instead "
"of the default `foo[0]=bar&foo[1]=baz`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/request_README.md:780
msgid ""
"`body` - entity body for PATCH, POST and PUT requests. Must be a "
"`Buffer`, `String` or `ReadStream`. If `json` is `true`, then `body` must"
" be a JSON-serializable object."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/request_README.md:781
msgid ""
"`form` - when passed an object or a querystring, this sets `body` to a "
"querystring representation of value, and adds `Content-type: "
"application/x-www-form-urlencoded` header. When passed no options, a "
"`FormData` instance is returned (and is piped to request). See \"Forms\" "
"section above."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/request_README.md:782
msgid ""
"`formData` - data to pass for a `multipart/form-data` request. See "
"[Forms](#forms) section above."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/request_README.md:784
msgid ""
"`multipart` - array of objects which contain their own headers and `body`"
" attributes. Sends a `multipart/related` request. See [Forms](#forms) "
"section above."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/request_README.md:787
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"Alternatively you can pass in an object `{chunked: false, data: []}` "
"where `chunked` is used to specify whether the request is sent in "
"[chunked transfer "
"encoding](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Chunked_transfer_encoding) In "
"non-chunked requests, data items with body streams are not allowed."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/request_README.md:791
msgid ""
"`preambleCRLF` - append a newline/CRLF before the boundary of your "
"`multipart/form-data` request."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/request_README.md:792
msgid ""
"`postambleCRLF` - append a newline/CRLF at the end of the boundary of "
"your `multipart/form-data` request."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/request_README.md:793
msgid ""
"`json` - sets `body` to JSON representation of value and adds `Content-"
"type: application/json` header. Additionally, parses the response body as"
" JSON."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/request_README.md:794
msgid ""
"`jsonReviver` - a [reviver function](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-"
"US/docs/Web/JavaScript/Reference/Global_Objects/JSON/parse) that will be "
"passed to `JSON.parse()` when parsing a JSON response body."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/request_README.md:795
msgid ""
"`jsonReplacer` - a [replacer function](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-"
"US/docs/Web/JavaScript/Reference/Global_Objects/JSON/stringify) that will"
" be passed to `JSON.stringify()` when stringifying a JSON request body."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/request_README.md:799
msgid ""
"`auth` - a hash containing values `user` || `username`, `pass` || "
"`password`, and `sendImmediately` (optional). See documentation above."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/request_README.md:800
msgid "`oauth` - options for OAuth HMAC-SHA1 signing. See documentation above."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/request_README.md:801
msgid ""
"`hawk` - options for [Hawk signing](https://github.com/hueniverse/hawk). "
"The `credentials` key must contain the necessary signing info, [see hawk "
"docs for details](https://github.com/hueniverse/hawk#usage-example)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/request_README.md:802
msgid ""
"`aws` - `object` containing AWS signing information. Should have the "
"properties `key`, `secret`, and optionally `session` (note that this only"
" works for services that require session as part of the canonical "
"string). Also requires the property `bucket`, unless you’re specifying "
"your `bucket` as part of the path, or the request doesn’t use a bucket "
"(i.e. GET Services). If you want to use AWS sign version 4 use the "
"parameter `sign_version` with value `4` otherwise the default is version "
"2. If you are using SigV4, you can also include a `service` property that"
" specifies the service name. **Note:** you need to `npm install aws4` "
"first."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/request_README.md:803
msgid ""
"`httpSignature` - options for the [HTTP Signature "
"Scheme](https://github.com/joyent/node-http-"
"signature/blob/master/http_signing.md) using [Joyent's "
"library](https://github.com/joyent/node-http-signature). The `keyId` and "
"`key` properties must be specified. See the docs for other options."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/request_README.md:807
msgid ""
"`followRedirect` - follow HTTP 3xx responses as redirects (default: "
"`true`). This property can also be implemented as function which gets "
"`response` object as a single argument and should return `true` if "
"redirects should continue or `false` otherwise."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/request_README.md:808
msgid ""
"`followAllRedirects` - follow non-GET HTTP 3xx responses as redirects "
"(default: `false`)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/request_README.md:809
msgid ""
"`followOriginalHttpMethod` - by default we redirect to HTTP method GET. "
"you can enable this property to redirect to the original HTTP method "
"(default: `false`)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/request_README.md:810
msgid "`maxRedirects` - the maximum number of redirects to follow (default: `10`)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/request_README.md:811
msgid ""
"`removeRefererHeader` - removes the referer header when a redirect "
"happens (default: `false`). **Note:** if true, referer header set in the "
"initial request is preserved during redirect chain."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/request_README.md:815
msgid ""
"`encoding` - encoding to be used on `setEncoding` of response data. If "
"`null`, the `body` is returned as a `Buffer`. Anything else **(including "
"the default value of `undefined`)** will be passed as the "
"[encoding](http://nodejs.org/api/buffer.html#buffer_buffer) parameter to "
"`toString()` (meaning this is effectively `utf8` by default). (**Note:** "
"if you expect binary data, you should set `encoding: null`.)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/request_README.md:816
msgid ""
"`gzip` - if `true`, add an `Accept-Encoding` header to request compressed"
" content encodings from the server (if not already present) and decode "
"supported content encodings in the response. **Note:** Automatic decoding"
" of the response content is performed on the body data returned through "
"`request` (both through the `request` stream and passed to the callback "
"function) but is not performed on the `response` stream (available from "
"the `response` event) which is the unmodified `http.IncomingMessage` "
"object which may contain compressed data. See example below."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/request_README.md:817
msgid ""
"`jar` - if `true`, remember cookies for future use (or define your custom"
" cookie jar; see examples section)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/request_README.md:821
msgid "`agent` - `http(s).Agent` instance to use"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/request_README.md:822
msgid "`agentClass` - alternatively specify your agent's class name"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/request_README.md:823
msgid ""
"`agentOptions` - and pass its options. **Note:** for HTTPS see [tls API "
"doc for TLS/SSL "
"options](http://nodejs.org/api/tls.html#tls_tls_connect_options_callback)"
" and the [documentation above](#using-optionsagentoptions)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/request_README.md:824
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"`forever` - set to `true` to use the [forever-"
"agent](https://github.com/request/forever-agent) **Note:** Defaults to "
"`http(s).Agent({keepAlive:true})` in node 0.12+"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/request_README.md:825
msgid ""
"`pool` - an object describing which agents to use for the request. If "
"this option is omitted the request will use the global agent (as long as "
"your options allow for it). Otherwise, request will search the pool for "
"your custom agent. If no custom agent is found, a new agent will be "
"created and added to the pool. **Note:** `pool` is used only when the "
"`agent` option is not specified."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/request_README.md:826
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"A `maxSockets` property can also be provided on the `pool` object to set "
"the max number of sockets for all agents created (ex: `pool: {maxSockets:"
" Infinity}`)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/request_README.md:827
msgid ""
"Note that if you are sending multiple requests in a loop and creating "
"multiple new `pool` objects, `maxSockets` will not work as intended. To "
"work around this, either use "
"[`request.defaults`](#requestdefaultsoptions) with your pool options or "
"create the pool object with the `maxSockets` property outside of the "
"loop."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/request_README.md:832
msgid ""
"`timeout` - integer containing number of milliseconds, controls two "
"timeouts."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/request_README.md:833
msgid ""
"**Read timeout**: Time to wait for a server to send response headers (and"
" start the response body) before aborting the request."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/request_README.md:834
msgid ""
"**Connection timeout**: Sets the socket to timeout after `timeout` "
"milliseconds of inactivity. Note that increasing the timeout beyond the "
"OS-wide TCP connection timeout will not have any effect ([the default in "
"Linux can be anywhere from 20-120 seconds][linux-timeout])"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/request_README.md:840
msgid "`localAddress` - local interface to bind for network connections."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/request_README.md:841
msgid ""
"`proxy` - an HTTP proxy to be used. Supports proxy Auth with Basic Auth, "
"identical to support for the `url` parameter (by embedding the auth info "
"in the `uri`)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/request_README.md:842
msgid ""
"`strictSSL` - if `true`, requires SSL certificates be valid. **Note:** to"
" use your own certificate authority, you need to specify an agent that "
"was created with that CA as an option."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/request_README.md:843
msgid ""
"`tunnel` - controls the behavior of [HTTP `CONNECT` "
"tunneling](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/HTTP_tunnel#HTTP_CONNECT_tunneling)"
" as follows:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/request_README.md:846
msgid ""
"`undefined` (default) - `true` if the destination is `https`, `false` "
"otherwise"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/request_README.md:847
msgid ""
"`true` - always tunnel to the destination by making a `CONNECT` request "
"to the proxy"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/request_README.md:849
msgid "`false` - request the destination as a `GET` request."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/request_README.md:850
msgid ""
"`proxyHeaderWhiteList` - a whitelist of headers to send to a tunneling "
"proxy."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/request_README.md:852
msgid ""
"`proxyHeaderExclusiveList` - a whitelist of headers to send exclusively "
"to a tunneling proxy and not to destination."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/request_README.md:857
msgid ""
"`time` - if `true`, the request-response cycle (including all redirects) "
"is timed at millisecond resolution. When set, the following properties "
"are added to the response object:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/request_README.md:858
msgid ""
"`elapsedTime` Duration of the entire request/response in milliseconds "
"(*deprecated*)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/request_README.md:859
msgid ""
"`responseStartTime` Timestamp when the response began (in Unix Epoch "
"milliseconds) (*deprecated*)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/request_README.md:860
msgid ""
"`timingStart` Timestamp of the start of the request (in Unix Epoch "
"milliseconds)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/request_README.md:861
msgid ""
"`timings` Contains event timestamps in millisecond resolution relative to"
" `timingStart`. If there were redirects, the properties reflect the "
"timings of the final request in the redirect chain:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/request_README.md:862
msgid ""
"`socket` Relative timestamp when the "
"[`http`](https://nodejs.org/api/http.html#http_event_socket) module's "
"`socket` event fires. This happens when the socket is assigned to the "
"request."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/request_README.md:863
msgid ""
"`lookup` Relative timestamp when the "
"[`net`](https://nodejs.org/api/net.html#net_event_lookup) module's "
"`lookup` event fires. This happens when the DNS has been resolved."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/request_README.md:864
msgid ""
"`connect`: Relative timestamp when the "
"[`net`](https://nodejs.org/api/net.html#net_event_connect) module's "
"`connect` event fires. This happens when the server acknowledges the TCP "
"connection."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/request_README.md:865
msgid ""
"`response`: Relative timestamp when the "
"[`http`](https://nodejs.org/api/http.html#http_event_response) module's "
"`response` event fires. This happens when the first bytes are received "
"from the server."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/request_README.md:866
msgid ""
"`end`: Relative timestamp when the last bytes of the response are "
"received."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/request_README.md:867
msgid ""
"`timingPhases` Contains the durations of each request phase. If there "
"were redirects, the properties reflect the timings of the final request "
"in the redirect chain:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/request_README.md:868
msgid "`wait`: Duration of socket initialization (`timings.socket`)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/request_README.md:869
msgid "`dns`: Duration of DNS lookup (`timings.lookup` - `timings.socket`)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/request_README.md:870
msgid "`tcp`: Duration of TCP connection (`timings.connect` - `timings.socket`)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/request_README.md:871
msgid ""
"`firstByte`: Duration of HTTP server response (`timings.response` - "
"`timings.connect`)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/request_README.md:872
msgid "`download`: Duration of HTTP download (`timings.end` - `timings.response`)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/request_README.md:873
msgid "`total`: Duration entire HTTP round-trip (`timings.end`)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/request_README.md:875
msgid ""
"`har` - a [HAR 1.2 Request "
"Object](http://www.softwareishard.com/blog/har-12-spec/#request), will be"
" processed from HAR format into options overwriting matching values *(see"
" the [HAR 1.2 section](#support-for-har-12) for details)*"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/request_README.md:876
msgid ""
"`callback` - alternatively pass the request's callback in the options "
"object"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/request_README.md:878
msgid "The callback argument gets 3 arguments:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/request_README.md:880
msgid ""
"An `error` when applicable (usually from "
"[`http.ClientRequest`](http://nodejs.org/api/http.html#http_class_http_clientrequest)"
" object)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/request_README.md:881
msgid ""
"An "
"[`http.IncomingMessage`](https://nodejs.org/api/http.html#http_class_http_incomingmessage)"
" object (Response object)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/request_README.md:882
msgid ""
"The third is the `response` body (`String` or `Buffer`, or JSON object if"
" the `json` option is supplied)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/request_README.md:889
msgid "Convenience methods"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/request_README.md:891
msgid ""
"There are also shorthand methods for different HTTP METHODs and some "
"other conveniences."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/request_README.md:894
msgid "request.defaults(options)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/request_README.md:896
msgid ""
"This method **returns a wrapper** around the normal request API that "
"defaults to whatever options you pass to it."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/request_README.md:899
msgid ""
"**Note:** `request.defaults()` **does not** modify the global request "
"API; instead, it **returns a wrapper** that has your default settings "
"applied to it."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/request_README.md:902
msgid ""
"**Note:** You can call `.defaults()` on the wrapper that is returned from"
" `request.defaults` to add/override defaults that were previously "
"defaulted."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/request_README.md:905
msgid "For example:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/request_README.md:919
msgid "request.METHOD()"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/request_README.md:921
msgid ""
"These HTTP method convenience functions act just like `request()` but "
"with a default method already set for you:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/request_README.md:923
msgid "*request.get()*: Defaults to `method: \"GET\"`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/request_README.md:924
msgid "*request.post()*: Defaults to `method: \"POST\"`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/request_README.md:925
msgid "*request.put()*: Defaults to `method: \"PUT\"`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/request_README.md:926
msgid "*request.patch()*: Defaults to `method: \"PATCH\"`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/request_README.md:927
msgid "*request.del() / request.delete()*: Defaults to `method: \"DELETE\"`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/request_README.md:928
msgid "*request.head()*: Defaults to `method: \"HEAD\"`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/request_README.md:929
msgid "*request.options()*: Defaults to `method: \"OPTIONS\"`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/request_README.md:931
msgid "request.cookie()"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/request_README.md:933
msgid "Function that creates a new cookie."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/request_README.md:938
msgid "request.jar()"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/request_README.md:940
msgid "Function that creates a new cookie jar."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/request_README.md:946
msgid "response.caseless.get('header-name')"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/request_README.md:948
msgid ""
"Function that returns the specified response header field using a [case-"
"insensitive match](https://tools.ietf.org/html/rfc7230#section-3.2)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/request_README.md:963
msgid "Debugging"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/request_README.md:965
msgid "There are at least three ways to debug the operation of `request`:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/request_README.md:967
msgid ""
"Launch the node process like `NODE_DEBUG=request node script.js` "
"(`lib,request,otherlib` works too)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/request_README.md:970
msgid ""
"Set `require('request').debug = true` at any time (this does the same "
"thing as #1)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/request_README.md:973
msgid ""
"Use the [request-debug module](https://github.com/request/request-debug) "
"to view request and response headers and bodies."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/request_README.md:981
msgid "Timeouts"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/request_README.md:983
msgid ""
"Most requests to external servers should have a timeout attached, in case"
" the server is not responding in a timely manner. Without a timeout, your"
" code may have a socket open/consume resources for minutes or more."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/request_README.md:987
msgid ""
"There are two main types of timeouts: **connection timeouts** and **read "
"timeouts**. A connect timeout occurs if the timeout is hit while your "
"client is attempting to establish a connection to a remote machine "
"(corresponding to the [connect() call][connect] on the socket). A read "
"timeout occurs any time the server is too slow to send back a part of the"
" response."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/request_README.md:993
msgid ""
"These two situations have widely different implications for what went "
"wrong with the request, so it's useful to be able to distinguish them. "
"You can detect timeout errors by checking `err.code` for an 'ETIMEDOUT' "
"value. Further, you can detect whether the timeout was a connection "
"timeout by checking if the `err.connect` property is set to `true`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/request_README.md:1011
msgid "Examples:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/request_README.md:1038
msgid ""
"For backwards-compatibility, response compression is not supported by "
"default. To accept gzip-compressed responses, set the `gzip` option to "
"`true`. Note that the body data passed through `request` is automatically"
" decompressed while the response object is unmodified and will contain "
"compressed data if the server sent a compressed response."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/request_README.md:1070
msgid ""
"Cookies are disabled by default (else, they would be used in subsequent "
"requests). To enable cookies, set `jar` to `true` (either in `defaults` "
"or `options`)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/request_README.md:1079
msgid ""
"To use a custom cookie jar (instead of `request`’s global cookie jar), "
"set `jar` to an instance of `request.jar()` (either in `defaults` or "
"`options`)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/request_README.md:1089
msgid "OR"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/request_README.md:1101
msgid ""
"To use a custom cookie store (such as a "
"[`FileCookieStore`](https://github.com/mitsuru/tough-cookie-filestore) "
"which supports saving to and restoring from JSON files), pass it as a "
"parameter to `request.jar()`:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/request_README.md:1116
msgid ""
"The cookie store must be a [`tough-"
"cookie`](https://github.com/SalesforceEng/tough-cookie) store and it must"
" support synchronous operations; see the [`CookieStore` API "
"docs](https://github.com/SalesforceEng/tough-cookie#api) for details."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/request_README.md:1122
msgid "To inspect your cookie jar after a request:"
msgstr ""

